<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Blackbeard</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1680–1718</span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a> · Also known as Edward Teach, Edward Thatch</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Blackbeard, Edward Teach or Thatch, was an English pirate of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caribbean">Caribbean</a> and the American coast. Associated with the pirate base at Nassau, he captured a French slave ship in 1717, renamed it Queen Anne's Revenge and blockaded Charleston in 1718. He was killed in a fight with a force sent by the governor of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/virginia">Virginia</a> off North Carolina in November 1718.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/blackbeard.jpg" alt="Blackbeard" width="320" height="460" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Joseph Nicholls (fl. 1726–55).[1] Although James Basire (1730–1802) is attributed as the engraver based on the signat... · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Edward_Teach_Commonly_Call%27d_Black_Beard_(bw)_(cropped).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
